  "question": "Can the Ding-mediated six-title route be tied to a contemporaneous Zhao Wanli publication, and which titles can be named without merging later retrospective traditions?",
  "answer": "Yes at a publication-text bridge level, not yet by direct inspection of the 1951 issue page. A first-party National Library of China review by Liu Peng bibliographically closes Zhao Wanli's 《永乐大典展览的意义——一九五一年八月北京图书馆举办》 to 《文物参考资料》1951年第9期, pp.221–233. Xiao Ling's 2026 scholarly article 《赵万里与古籍保护》 quotes the relevant passage through 《赵万里文集：第一卷》 (国家图书馆出版社, 2011, p.197): Ding Huikang donated six titles, explicitly including a Song edition of 《东家杂记》 and a Yuan edition of 《太平乐府》. The remaining four titles, direct 1951 wording, and identity with HC's Ding Fubao six-title retrospective remain unresolved.",
